26
00:02:30.453 --> 00:02:39.873
(narrator) Then preference tuning: two answers for mean, one that hedges and one that sounds sure; people vote for the sure one, which crashes on an empty list.

27
00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.900
♪ Post-training brought a teacher with answers, task by task: ♪

28
00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.400
♪ Textbook problems? Aced them all! But is that what you ask? ♪

29
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.460
♪ In Reinforcement Learning, on tasks a test could score, ♪

30
00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.620
♪ I learned to pass whatever's checked, not what the test is for. ♪

31
00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.880
♪ Preference Tuning: where no test can check if it is true, ♪

32
00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.833
♪ People picked the smoothest talker, so I sound sure to you. ♪

33
00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.013
